work_units.notes:
Update `benchbox/core/results/driver_metadata.py` so the shared helper
can also populate `result.platform_info` using the same `setdefault()`
behavior currently present in runner-local `_apply_driver_meta_to_dicts()`.

Preserve these semantics:
  - adapter values win over database config values;
  - config values fill only missing adapter values;
  - `driver_version_resolved` falls back to requested `driver_version`;
  - `driver_package` and `driver_version_requested` in execution metadata
    use `setdefault`;
  - `driver_auto_install_used` remains recorded even when false;
  - platform_info population never overwrites existing platform metadata.
